DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((e^(x)))^2");
$fun_1 = Formula("(((((x)^(1/4)))^(1/4)))^(1/2)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-10, -6, -3, 0} - (1, 13))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("[5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -6, -3, 0}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [5, infinity))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 11] U (3, 8) U ((3, infinity) U (3, 8))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(3, 8) U (-infinity, 11]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

Lily collected [`1`] seashell on Monday, [`11`] seashells on Tuesday, and [`13`] seashells on Wednesday. On Thursday, she gave [`10`] seashells to her friend for an art project. How many seashells does Lily have left?

[_____]{15}
[%
1+11+13-10

First, add the seashells from Monday and Tuesday: 1 + 11 = 12 seashells. Then, add Wednesday's seashells: 12 + 13 = 25 seashells. Finally, subtract the seashells given away: 25 - 10 = 15 seashells.
%]
---

Tom had [`13`] trading cards in his collection. For his birthday, he received [`9`] packages from his cousins, with each package containing [`9`] trading cards. How many trading cards does Tom have now?

[_____]{94}
[%
13+9*9

First, calculate the trading cards from the packages: 9 × 9 = 81 trading cards. Then, add the cards he originally had: 13 + 81 = 94 trading cards.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 2\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 < x < 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 11\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B \cup (A \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -6, -3, 0\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 5\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 1 < x < 13\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 7, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -7, 9, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 7, 0>") x Compute("<-7, 9, 3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, 7, 0>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, 3>") x Compute("<3, 7, 0>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, 9, 3>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, -9, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 10, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -2, 0, -9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 0, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, 0, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-8, -9, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, -9, 10>") x Compute("<8, 10, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-8, -9, 10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<8, 10, -5>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
